<article class="env-lemma" id="02U8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02U8">Lemma <span data-tag="02U8">42.38.5</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $X$, $Y$ be locally of finite type over $S$. Let $\mathcal{E}$ be a finite locally free sheaf of rank $r$ on $Y$. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a flat morphism of relative dimension $r$. Let $\alpha $ be a $k$-cycle on $Y$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  f^*(c_ j(\mathcal{E}) \cap \alpha ) = c_ j(f^*\mathcal{E}) \cap f^*\alpha  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Write $\alpha _ j = c_ j(\mathcal{E}) \cap \alpha $, so $\alpha _0 = \alpha $. By Lemma <a href="/tag/02U6" data-tag="02U6">42.38.2</a> we have 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \sum \nolimits _{i = 0}^ r (-1)^ i c_1(\mathcal{O}_ P(1))^ i \cap \pi ^*(\alpha _{r - i}) = 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       in the chow group of the projective bundle $(\pi : P \to Y, \mathcal{O}_ P(1))$ associated to $\mathcal{E}$. Consider the fibre product diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ P_ X = \mathbf{P}(f^*\mathcal{E}) \ar[r]_-{f'} \ar[d]_{\pi _ X} &  P \ar[d]^\pi \\  X \ar[r]^ f &  Y }  \]
</div>
    <p>
       Note that $\mathcal{O}_{P_ X}(1)$ is the pullback of $\mathcal{O}_ P(1)$. Apply flat pullback $(f')^*$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/02S1" data-tag="02S1">42.20.2</a>) to the displayed equation above. By Lemmas <a href="/tag/02SS" data-tag="02SS">42.26.2</a> and <a href="/tag/02RD" data-tag="02RD">42.14.3</a> we see that 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \sum \nolimits _{i = 0}^ r (-1)^ i c_1(\mathcal{O}_{P_ X}(1))^ i \cap \pi _ X^*(f^*\alpha _{r - i}) = 0  \]
</div>
    <p>
       holds in the chow group of $P_ X$. By the characterization of Lemma <a href="/tag/02U6" data-tag="02U6">42.38.2</a> we conclude. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>